From cf0db0b8dae701a47d3c043fd7bc25b96e7b3676 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:32:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] CUDA: GP100: multi-column Q3_K and large-matrix Q8_0
 MMVQ; softplus fusion for batched decode

Three shapes that still left the fp16 path (0007-0011) when a matmul has 2..8
columns (MTP verification, several sequences decoding at once):

- Q3_K had no multi-column kernel. Each row's 32 weights per thread are now
  unpacked once and every column FMA'd against them, with activation reads
  made unconditional (clamped super-block) so they are shared across rows.
  The Q3_K MTP draft head at 4 sequences: 0.83 -> 0.48 ms per step.
- Q8_0 gets the same treatment on gp100_mmvq_b32's staging, for matrices of
  >= 2048 rows only: at 4 columns it wins there (0.178 -> 0.085 ms) and loses
  on small ones, which keep the generic kernel. IQ4_NL shares the kernel but
  is not dispatched to it (slower than the generic one).
- The ADD -> SOFTPLUS -> MUL fusion of gated delta-net layers now accepts the
  per-head bias/scale broadcast over sequences, instead of falling back to
  three launches in batched decode. Same ops in the same order; bit-identical.

2x P100, -sm tensor, Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL (Q3_K MTP head), on top of 0011:
llama-batched-bench decode, 4 sequences 86.8 -> 88.3 tok/s aggregate (+1.7%),
1 sequence unchanged. test-backend-ops passes; decode-path KLD vs a Q8_0
reference: -ub 1 unchanged (0.011261), -ub 5 0.011278 (MTP verification).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
